{
  "dom_id": "step-q143753",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "In a gas station, $40%$ of the clients buy Regular gasoline, $45%$ buy Premium gasoline, and $15%$ buy Supreme gasoline. If $65%$ of the clients that purchase Regular gasoline paid with a credit card, $50%$ of the clients that buy Premium gasoline paid with a credit card, and $60%$ of the clients that buy Supreme gasoline paid with a credit card,  what is the probability that a randomly selected client paid with a credit card?",
  "worked_solution": "Let  $C$ be the event that the client paid with a credit card, and\n\n- let $R$ be the event that the client bought Regular gasoline,\n\n- let $Q$  be the event that the client bought Premium gasoline,\n\n- let $S$ be the event that the client bought Supreme gasoline.\n\nThen the disjoint union $R⊔Q⊔S$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected client paid with a credit card, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(C) & =P(C\\cap R)+P(C\\cap Q)+P(C\\cap S) \\\\  & =P(C|R)P(R)+P(C|Q)P(Q)+P(C|S)P(S)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since $40%$ of the clients buy Regular gasoline, $45%$ of the clients buy Premium gasoline, and $15%$ of the clients buy Supreme gasoline, we have\n\n$$\nP(R)=0.4,\\,P(Q)=0.45,\\,P(S)=0.15.\n$$\n\n- Since $65%$ of the clients that buy Regular gasoline, $50%$ of the clients that buy Premium gasoline, and $60%$ of the clients that buy Supreme gasoline,  paid with a credit card, we have\n\n$$\nP(C|R)=0.65,\\,P(C|Q)=0.5,\\,P(C|S)=0.6.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected client paid with a credit card is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(C) & =P(C|R)P(R)+P(C|Q)P(Q)+P(C|S)P(S) \\\\  & =(0.65)(0.4)+(0.5)(0.45)+(0.6)(0.15) \\\\  & =0.26+0.225+0.009 \\\\  & =0.575.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
